fe35d87c7553fd23e8aab3a1dde7e712f286b416
# ^ The AB-JChess commit the prod image runs (scripts/engine-assets.sh reads the
# first line; this comment is ignored).
#
# AB-JChess (https://github.com/lxsgx23/AB-JChess, GPL-3, by lxsgx23) is a
# Pikafish-derived jieqi engine with its own NNUE. fe35d87c is release v0.2d
# (2026-10-10): the source moved to abjchess/src and reads a new net format
# (ABJCHESSV11). Measured against v0.2b, the pin before it, at our live 4 s/move
# and 4 threads over 300 games: +54 Elo [+16, +93] (mistboard-engine
# lab/jieqi-match/abj-0.2d-vs-0.2b). v0.2b had beaten the PikaJieQi pin by +92
# over 400 games (lab/jieqi-abjchess-2026-09-29/run6-v02b-4s.jsonl).
#
# Only the binary is built here. The net is NOT in our engines release: the
# author allowed site use (lxsgx23/AB-JChess#1, 2026-09-30) on the terms that we
# fetch it from his release and never re-host it, so railpack.json downloads his
# v0.2d zip at image build time and checks the zip's and the net's sha256.
# Moving this pin means re-reading his release for the matching net.
#
# Built with clang for x86-64-avx2 (engine-assets.sh ABJ_ARCH), not the shared
# sse41 target: all its strength is the net, and the NNUE runs several times
# slower without AVX2. Prod web measured 2026-09-30: AMD EPYC 9655, avx2 bmi2
# avx512 present.
